    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A partial return changes the second distance.\n\nA→B is x km downstream. Then the boat returns upstream only to the midpoint, so the second leg is x/2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "With river speeds 18 down and 10 up, and total time 19 h:\n\nx/18 + x/20 = 19\n19x/180 = 19\nx = 180 km.\n\nThe trap is using x for both legs.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
